msgid "Chord Construction"
msgstr ""

#: ../../SerialAPI.rst:508
msgid ""
"There are 128-bits in a chord. The first 8 bits will typically be 0x00, "
"as this byte value is used to store an index value for chordmaps where "
"the chord output is longer than what can be stored in memory in a single "
"chordmap, which has 192 bytes allocated per memory entry."
msgstr ""

#: ../../SerialAPI.rst:510
msgid ""
"The next 120-bit bits are segmented into twelve 10-bit chunks. Each "
"10-bit value is a 10-bit CC action code. While CC action codes can "
"reference up to 13-bits, only up to 10-bit values can be used for key "
"inputs. The key inputs for a chord are sorted in descending order from "
"greatest in value to least in value."
msgstr ""

